#!/bin/bash

# The focused-window border, drawn by JankyBorders.
#
# Built to look like it belongs to the bar above it rather than to a different
# theme. The bar is graphite pills with a white hairline and white text; the
# border is that same white, at a width that reads from across the room and no
# wider. It was a 6pt gold glow before, which was the loudest thing on the
# screen and the one element that shared no colour with anything else, and a
# 6pt stroke eats into small windows at the corners.
#
# Only the focused window gets one. An unfocused border in any colour answers a
# question nobody asks, the 16pt gaps already separate the tiles, and the less
# there is around the others the more the one that matters stands out. It is
# fully transparent rather than turned off, because borders keeps drawing
# inactive windows either way and transparent is the one colour that costs
# nothing to look at.
#
# 3pt at 95% white. 2pt was tried first and was right in colour and wrong in
# weight: on a dark window over a dark wallpaper it read as the window's own
# edge rather than as a mark of focus. 3 is where it starts to say "this one"
# from across the room without turning back into a frame. `hidpi=on` so the
# stroke is drawn at retina resolution on the built-in instead of being
# upscaled into a soft band.
options=(
  style=round
  width=3.0
  hidpi=on
  active_color=0xf2f5f5f7
  inactive_color=0x00000000
)
borders "${options[@]}"
